==English==

===Alternative spellings===
*[[pandar]]

===Etymology===
From Chaucer's character '''[[w:Pandarus|Pandare]]''' (in ''[[w:Troilus and Criseyde|Troilus and Criseyde]]''), from Italian '''[[w:Pandarus|Pandaro]]''' (found in [[w:Boccaccio|Boccaccio]]), from Latin '''[[w:Pandarus|Pandarus]]''', from Greek '''[[Πάνδαρος]]'''. (See also Shakespeare's [[wikibooks:Troilus and Cressida|Troilus and Cressida]])

